<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.8.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01875</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.8.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f048b8c6-a81a-459d-b163-bfe6e6cb9d6f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="9694b95a-1c6f-4013-87ea-8a5e1a43d72e" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="13e5d43f-0171-4ebf-bf68-39abef4954ec" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((2x+5)(x+3)\) is equivalent to \(2x^2+11x+15\)." data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((2x+5)(x+3)\\) is equivalent to \\(2x^2+5x+8\\).&quot;, &quot;\\((2x +5)(x +3)\\) is equivalent to \\(2x^2+14x + 23\\).&quot;, &quot;\\((2x+5)(x+3)\\) is equivalent to \\(2x^2+11x+15\\).&quot;,&quot;\\((2x +5)(x +3)\\) is equivalent to \\(30x^2\\). &quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Choose the expression that best describes the diagram.<figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a4c39cadbd12167dc25e8a8977547823585c8403"/></media></figure></para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \((2x+5)(x+3)\) is equivalent to \(2x^2+11x+15\).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="279bb73a-6893-4a2d-b527-807bee0fa839" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((x+8)(x+4)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((x+2)(x+6)\\) &quot;, &quot;\\((x+4)(x+2)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+8)(x+4)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+2)(x+3)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>In questions a–d, match each expanded quadratic expression with an equivalent expression written as a product.</para>
      <para>\(x^2+12x+32\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \((x+8)(x+4)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="8e7633c5-78da-49c3-b6a7-e6265f139b84" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((x+2)(x+3)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((x+2)(x+6)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+4)(x+2)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+8)(x+4)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+2)(x+3)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> \(x^2+5x+6\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \((x+2)(x+3)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="5d9dd332-aeb9-4237-affe-cd381e9dd585" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((x+4)(x+2)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((x+2)(x+6)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+4)(x+2)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+8)(x+4)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+2)(x+3)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2+6x+8\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \((x+4)(x+2)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2d-->
  <exercise data-content-id="224fe3bf-30c3-4dc2-a62b-aaa67c1a3c84" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((x+2)(x+6)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((x+2)(x+6)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+4)(x+2)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+8)(x+4)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+2)(x+3)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2+8x+12\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \((x+2)(x+6)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a598cde7-4fc5-490f-833a-0b5c704e9fcf" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;\\(x(x+4)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+2)^2-4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+4)x\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(x(x+4)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+2)^2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+x)(x+4)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+2)^2-4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+4)x\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para><emphasis>Select three </emphasis>expressions that are equivalent to \(x^2+4x\).</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(x(x+4)\), \((x+2)^2-4\), \((x+4)x\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.8.2-7.8.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--4a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="5fc3f3a4-158c-4131-977c-33bba99944f5" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="Tyler added 5 and 2 and 5 and 3 instead of multiplying them." data-solution-options="[&quot;Tyler added 5 and 2 and 5 and 3 instead of multiplying them.&quot;, &quot;Tyler multiplied 5 and 2 and 5 and 3 instead of adding them.&quot;, &quot;Tyler should have labeled the top \\(2x\\) and 5 and the side \\(x\\) and 3.&quot;, &quot;Tyler should have labeled the top \\(x\\) and 3 and the side \\(2x\\) and 5.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Tyler drew a diagram to expand \((x+5)(2x+3)\).</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="Rectangle partitioned into 4 smaller rectangles. The top is labeled 2 x and 3. The side is labeled x and 5. Inside, the top row contains 2 x squared and 3 x. The bottom row contains 7 x and 8."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/3257ad167a891e11df938a70502ad9c0fd909998"/></media></figure></para>
      <para> Tyler’s diagram is incorrect. Choose the sentence that describes Tyler’s mistake.</para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Tyler added 5 and 2 and 5 and 3 instead of multiplying them. </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.4.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--4b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="740ac6b4-bf17-4ecd-ae4e-ae1e88a74c1f" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(2x^2+13x+15\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(3x+8\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(30x^2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(2x^2+10x+8\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(2x^2+13x+15\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> What is the correct expanded form of \((x+5)(2x+3)\)?</para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(2x^2+13x+15\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div>
  </div></section>
</content>
